claims:
1. A method comprising:
determining, at a server, predicted depths of a first point cloud from a first device;
determining, at the server, predicted depths of a second point cloud from a second device;
determining, at the server, a relative pose between a first reference coordinate frame of the first device and a second reference coordinate frame of the second device by registering the first point cloud with the second point cloud based on corresponding predicted depths; and
providing the relative pose to the first device and the second device.

20. A non-transitory computer-readable storage medium, the computer-readable storage medium including instructions that when executed by a server, cause the server to perform operations comprising:
determining predicted depths of a first point cloud from a first device;
determining predicted depths of a second point cloud from a second device;
determining a relative pose between a first reference coordinate frame of the first device and a second reference coordinate frame of the second device by registering the first point cloud with the second point cloud based on corresponding predicted depths; and
providing the relative pose to the first device and the second device.
